{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 29,
  "title": "At the market",
  "description": "Name the people and the things at a market stall.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "A market is people and objects. The nouns are ordinary ones, but they are the words a learner hears first when they go shopping for food.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El vendedor, el cliente, el carrito, el toldo, el almacén and el ticket are masculine. La bandeja, la báscula, la etiqueta and la fila are feminine. A folder is la carpeta, and the scale that weighs your shopping is la báscula.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el vendedor",
            "en": "the seller"
          },
          {
            "es": "la báscula",
            "en": "the scale"
          },
          {
            "es": "la fila",
            "en": "the queue"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Words that change in the plural",
        "body": "The plural adds -s or -es: el vendedor becomes los vendedores and la etiqueta becomes las etiquetas. Two words lose the accent in the plural: el almacén becomes los almacenes and la etiqueta becomes las etiquetas.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "los vendedores",
            "en": "the sellers"
          },
          {
            "es": "las etiquetas",
            "en": "the labels"
          },
          {
            "es": "hay mucha gente en la fila",
            "en": "there are a lot of people in the queue"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
